"\nTARGET 50 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_09\u002dwork_logs/2026_09_10\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY bd46dafc2920889d6569ec298e75fc28bc89dd69 5dc8e97ebaae90c01915b99c77963cbb724777ea7c7f60fbb94578dd9ba45dec RANGES [[617, 639]] MASKED [617, 622]\n617: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n618: \n619: Maintainer: \"116 to 52 to 71 to 39 and then ... 74 and 100 ... with the\n620: same build.\" Two of the six were already fixed in code and only needed\n621: proving (#39's rule order, #74's sibling folders); two were small and sharp\n622: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n623: line); one needed a decision written down and a restore\u002dside sentence\n624: (#52); one needed its harness assertions (#100). Everything is proven by a\n625: test that will run again: four new round\u002dtrip steps, one new bwrap case,\n626: and the shipped script reproducing #71's leak before the fix closed it.\n627: \n628: Three things the harness taught while the steps were written: the suite's\n629: device may have no `REMOTENAME` in its conf (the scripts fall back to the\n630: first configured remote, so the harness must too); the suite's saves folder\n631: can sit at the cloud root (`/GAMES`), where by design there is no parent to\n632: tell \"empty\" from \"wrong\", so the empty\u002dcloud step uses a folder of its own;\n633: and a settings backup with nothing local to send exits 0 saying so, so a\n634: step that wants an upload has to plant an archive first. And one thing\n635: `cloud_migrate_layout` taught: its idea of \"current\" was one layout, when\n636: CHANGE CLOUD FOLDER has been writing another on purpose since #74.\n637: \n638: Built as ES `f48bc3620` / `88b82d94a7`; images building.\n\nTARGET 51 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_09\u002dwork_logs/2026_09_11\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY 13ba8fc817a80fa72a8e88e52e790a96069523b8 3c244f161e368ef35fe522b9eb9a72ffd1573f313ad2de7880650fe3f7e63bd4 RANGES [[350, 372]] MASKED []\n350: ## 23:05 UTC \u002d\u002d the council ran, three and a half hours, and chose store\u002dfirst\n351: \n352: Five seats, eight gates, every one PASS. The maintainer asked whether a\n353: run that fast was real; it was Step 1 of six, and a 17\u002dsource corpus\n354: against last week's 42 is why each step took twenty minutes rather than\n355: an hour. Step 2 taught one thing about the tooling: Kimi returned a\n356: 2284\u002dbyte review cut mid\u002dsentence after four attempts and the Facilitator\n357: called it success; the orchestrator has to read the body, not the exit\n358: code. Re\u002dinvoked once, kept both, logged both.\n359: \n360: The vote went 3\u002d2 to Claude's plan over Kimi's, and the two dissenters\n361: were right about the engineering: Claude had the invariant (store\u002dfirst)\n362: and Kimi had the transaction shape, the migration and the build order.\n363: The consensus round, briefed with the maintainer's post\u002dvote steer (time\n364: to play, bandwidth, round trips; sync no longer than it must be; the\n365: save's sanctity as the floor), kept the invariant and integrated the\n366: rest: ten blockers cleared, ten more provisions taken by filename, twelve\n367: conflicts stated rather than averaged, thirteen proposals for the\n368: maintainer. Step 5 turned the handoff into tracker text for #134, #22,\n369: #23, #25 and two new children. Nothing is applied to the tracker or built\n370: until the maintainer has read it. 2.47M tokens.\n371: \n\nTARGET 52 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_09\u002dwork_logs/2026_09_12\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY dd898e922b6adca4c9349b18cef2a7a8b196ce64 4fd2c5736f9df7b0f8c69d1c0fb6847befa3b3774a0bca3d0f05adb65de287cc RANGES [[667, 694]] MASKED []\n667: ## 23:30 UTC \u002d\u002d the tracker\u002dhygiene pass, and the runs that closed its last boxes\n668: \n669: The maintainer's step one: close the delivered issues. An agent read 23\n670: candidates body\u002dand